## Fix R2RML generation when ontology URIs contain spaces

Context: R2RML Turtle serialization failed (502) when the domain/ontology
name contained spaces (e.g. "WRFM - Shell"). Changing ontology.base_uri alone
did not rewrite stale class/property/mapping IRIs that still carried spaces.
RDFLib then refused to serialize those URIRefs.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/w3c/r2rml/R2RMLGenerator.py
   Percent-encode illegal IRI characters in base_uri and all config-derived URIRefs before Turtle serialization.
2. src/back/objects/domain/Domain.py
   Sanitize auto-generated and custom base URIs; replace non-IRI-safe chars in domain names used for auto base_uri.
3. tests/units/mapping/test_r2rml_generator.py
   Cover spaced base_uri init and generation with a spaced class URI.
4. tests/units/domain/test_domain_service.py
   Cover auto/custom base_uri sanitization for names and URIs with spaces.

